###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# DFT relaxations were allowed up to 144 hours on 12 cores each; training
# cost of the baselines was not captured from the parts read.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy errors are MAEs of total system energies referenced as adsorption energies, in eV per structure (not per atom).
# - Not encoded: the IS2RE and IS2RS tasks (Tables 3, 4, 12, 14), the force-only and energy-only variants and DimeNet++-Large of Table 13, force cosine and EFwT metrics, the test-set results, and the models trained on the smaller S2EF subsets.
# - SchNet and CGCNN hyperparameters (Tables 6 and 7) were not read; only the DimeNet++ S2EF column of Table 8 is encoded. 'Number of hidden channels' 192 is encoded as numFeatures, 'number of interaction blocks' 3 as numLayers, 'number of spherical harmonics' 7 as numAngularBasis.
# - CGCNN is a new registry method (it is used here as an energy and force model); DimeNet++ is encoded under entity:DimeNet.
# - The four validation splits are modelled as material systems so that errors group by split.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

